1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,830
2,000 AI detectives just searched
7.7 million mouse brain cells… in 32 minutes.

2
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:10,120
And one of them found a
clue nobody had connected.

3
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:11,230
Picture a city.

4
00:00:11,230 --> 00:00:15,140
7.7 million houses: those
are the brain cells.

5
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,050
Their wiring: the genes.

6
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:19,390
Scientists cut one wire in each house,

7
00:00:19,390 --> 00:00:21,710
with a gene-editing tool called CRISPR.

8
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:25,450
Nearly 2,000 different wires,
all linked to disease.

9
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:27,260
Then they photographed every house,

10
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:30,260
to see which lights stayed
on… and which went dark.

11
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:31,140
The result?

12
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,810
A mountain of photos.

13
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:36,650
One wire at a time, that's
months of work… maybe a year.

14
00:00:36,650 --> 00:00:40,580
So OpenAI sent in the detectives:
copies of its biology AI,

15
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:42,140
GPT-Rosalind.

16
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:44,390
One detective for every cut wire.

17
00:00:44,390 --> 00:00:46,920
Each one studied its
houses, read the research,

18
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:48,360
and wrote a case report.

19
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:52,860
Given the same job, one AI
on its own cited 11 papers.

20
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:53,620
The team?

21
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:55,510
Over 7,000.

22
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:59,180
First test: could they find what
the scientists had already found…

23
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:00,660
without seeing their paper?

24
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:01,480
They could.

25
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:04,920
In blind tests, experts preferred
the team over the lone AI,

26
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:06,390
3 times out of 4.

27
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:07,990
Then… the clue.

28
00:01:07,990 --> 00:01:12,860
One wire, DCTN1, runs the
delivery lorries inside neurons.

29
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:16,980
In houses where that wire was cut, the
cholesterol-making genes switched on.

30
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:20,860
Like a town whose deliveries stop…
so it starts baking its own bread.

31
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:21,560
Why?

32
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,630
Earlier research suggests that
when cholesterol can't be moved,

33
00:01:24,630 --> 00:01:25,970
cells make more.

34
00:01:25,970 --> 00:01:29,920
And when DCTN1 breaks in people,
it causes Perry syndrome:

35
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:32,700
a rare brain disease with
Parkinson's-like symptoms.

36
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:35,700
So maybe the problem isn't
too little cholesterol.

37
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:38,080
Maybe it's cholesterol in the wrong place.

38
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:41,120
Fix the deliveries… and maybe
you protect the neurons.

39
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,530
But careful: it's a lead, not a cure.

40
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:45,760
It's from mice, it isn't
peer-reviewed yet,

41
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,630
and a lab still has to test it.

42
00:01:47,630 --> 00:01:50,000
The AI didn't run a single experiment.

43
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,090
It connected dots in evidence
humans had already gathered.

44
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:54,840
2,000 detectives.

45
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,950
32 minutes.

46
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:57,720
One clue worth chasing.

47
00:01:57,720 --> 00:02:00,450
Follow for more AI, explained like this.
